        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0152" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">722.2315/1303</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 581</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-07-21">July 21,
                        1939</date>.<lb/>[Received July 28.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on July
                    19th <hi rendition="#italic">El Comercio</hi> of Quito published a press
                    despatch stating that an incident had taken place on the Ecuadoran-Peruvian
                    frontier between Ecuadoran and Peruvian troops. The incident occurred at 10
                    o’clock on the morning of July 18th in the Province of El Oro south of a point
                    called Aguas Verdes in the Pocitos region. The press reported that several
                    persons had been killed and wounded.</p>
                <p>Further details published on July 20th indicated that although no one had been
                    killed or wounded, the Peruvians claimed that Ecuadoran troops had fired on
                    members of the Peruvian Civil Guard, whereas the Ecuadorans stated that they had
                    been fired on first.</p>
                <p>The Ecuadoran Minister in Lima was instructed to present a formal protest to the
                    Peruvian Government for this violation of the <hi rendition="#italic">status
                        quo</hi> and invasion of Ecuadoran territory by the Peruvian Army. The
                    Government of Peru likewise instructed its Chargé d’Affaires at Quito to present
                    a protest to the Ecuadoran Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>An official communiqué of the Foreign Office, a translation of which is enclosed,
                    gives a complete account of the Ecuadoran version of the incident.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Boaz Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d193-a1.xml" xpointer="d193-a1"/>
